Z||000000||My7Fieros||10-01-2000||09:14 PM||||I know this has prob. been posted before, but I just noticed (first time Ive been through a tank of gas on this car) that my car is out of gas when it gets to the 1/4 tank mark...how do I fix?<P>oops! sorry, thought I was in T D & Q.....<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 10-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fearless Freep||10-01-2000||09:17 PM||||Mine does the same thing.  Course the simple fix is to just fill the tank up completely, then carefully remove the gas needle and stick (glue) it back to the full line (if yours is like mine, the needle shoots WAY past the full line)||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||10-01-2000||09:20 PM||||Hey Fearless, yeah my guage shot way past the full guage when I filled her up..heres the thing though, Ive put 15 miles on her and now it reads at the full mark...jeez, I hope she dosnt get THAT bad of gas milage!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fearless Freep||10-01-2000||09:23 PM||||Yeah...I can relate to that as well....I drive 165 miles per day.  The gas mileage is definately on my mind come 5pm rush hour/traffic jam||||reg||1
Z||000004||DjKid||10-01-2000||09:27 PM||||My 88 was like that when I got her... I replaced the gastank&sending thingie.. still no change... so I swapped the gas gauge off my 87.. and she's been working sweet ever since.. but be warned, when I swapped the gause.. hehe.. my stupid self ran out of gas the next day..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Ray - Blue 88 Coupe - <A HREF="http://blueknight.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank>My Blue Knight</A> - <A HREF="http://www.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank> Carolina Fieros</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fearless Freep||10-01-2000||09:32 PM||||DJ....done that one too!  First week I had my car it started sputtering.  After running around the engine with my tool kit and saying every 4 letter word. just casually looked at the gas gauge and it kept saying I had 1/4 tank..........thank goodness for the 1 gallon can of gas out back.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cheever2||10-01-2000||09:55 PM||||Both of my 88's do that.  Somebody's got a site describing how to fix it, but I'm too lazy for what they said to do.  Can't remember where it was.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||WisconsinGT||10-01-2000||11:37 PM||||Qnother anomaly at least on my 88GT is that I can get about 150 miles out of a half a tank of gas. But boy does that last half a tank go fast. I total about 220 on a tank af gas. FWIW||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fformula88||10-02-2000||05:38 PM||||My tank is empty at 1/4 too.  Except sometimes, it will go back up to full after its down to a half a tank (about 90 miles after fillup) then go back down again.  I am assuming its the sending unit in the tank, but am not all that motivated to play around the gas tank.  However, if it is the guage I would definately replace it!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/Motorcity/Boulevard/9278/fierosig1.jpg">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||1
Z||000009||Songman||10-02-2000||06:04 PM||||My 88 coupe is empty at just about 1/8 of a tank... My girlfriend drives the car and I told her never to go below 1/4 tank! I figured it was just my car.<P>Wonder if my $500 88 Formula I bought this weekend will have the problem too. Sounds like most 88s did...||||reg||1
Z||000010||rockcrawl||10-02-2000||06:09 PM||||I've got an 86 that does it, never bothered trying to fix it. I also had an 85 that did it, a new (used) sending unit in the tank fixed that one. <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||12
Z||000011||Black88GT||10-02-2000||07:02 PM||||The sending unit in the tank is usually the problem.  Sometimes as someone mentioned its the actual gauge.  ||||reg||1
